<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 19 October, from 202 BCE to 1987.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">202 BCE</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Scipio defeats Hannibal at Zama</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Publius Cornelius Scipio defeated Hannibal near Zama in North Africa; 19 October is the traditional date. The victory ended the Second Punic War, leaving Rome dominant in the western Mediterranean.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1216</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">King John dies at Newark Castle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King John died of dysentery at Newark during a civil war with his barons and a French invasion. His nine-year-old son became Henry III, and his regents reissued Magna Carta to win back support.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1781</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cornwallis's army surrenders at Yorktown</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Besieged by American and French forces, Lord Cornwallis's army of about 8,000 surrendered at Yorktown, Virginia. The defeat effectively ended major fighting in the American Revolutionary War.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1813</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon retreats after defeat at Leipzig</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of the Nations ended with Napoleon's army in retreat from Leipzig, its rearguard trapped when a bridge was blown too early. He lost control of Germany, and the Allies invaded France within months.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1987</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Black Monday: stock markets crash worldwide</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Dow Jones Industrial Average fell 508 points, or 22.6 per cent, its largest one-day percentage fall. Markets crashed worldwide, though the wider economy recovered far faster than after 1929.</p></li></ol>
